      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "The term 'scaling laws' here means precision/size Pareto trade-offs for quantized models, not the Kaplan/Hoffmann loss laws. The reader's V6 'supports' label is dropped. Size differences across rows come from off-the-shelf models with different pretraining, and the recorded baseline (FP at the same size) measures the quantization gap rather than scaling."
  },
